266 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 564 0 R/E(How do I know if I am truly ready to buy? Financial readiness includes having a steady income, a reliable record of paying bills, and manageable long-term debt. Emotionally, you may be ready if you find yourself needing more space or wanting the freedom to personalize your own home.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

267 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 565 0 R/E(What is a mortgage pre-approval, and why is it important? A pre-approval is a letter from a lender stating how much they are willing to lend you based on your financial history. It is vital because it helps you shop within your budget and proves to sellers that you are a serious, qualified buyer.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

268 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 566 0 R/E(How much down payment do I really need? While 20% is ideal to avoid mortgage insurance, many first-time buyer programs allow for as little as 3% down. Some government-backed loans, like VA or USDA loans, even offer 0% down options for eligible buyers.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

269 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 567 0 R/E(What are closing costs? These are fees paid at the end of the transaction, typically ranging from 2% to 5% of the purchase price. They cover items like loan origination, title searches, appraisals, and government taxes.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

270 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 568 0 R/E(Can I back out if the home inspection reveals issues? Yes, if your contract includes an inspection contingency, you can negotiate for repairs, ask for a price credit, or cancel the sale without penalty if an agreement cannot be reached.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

271 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 569 0 R/E(How long does it take to close on a home? A: Once your offer is accepted, the typical timeline is 30 to 45 days. This allows time for inspections, the appraisal, and for your lender to finalize the paperwork)/Pg 18 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

